# Build output at the repo root. The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `si`
# also matches the SOURCE DIRECTORY cmd/si/, hiding every file in it from
# `git add`. cmd/si/main.go is tracked and stays tracked whatever this file
# says, so nothing was lost — but the next file added beside it would have been
# skipped in silence. Same trap the /si-test line below was already anchored for.
/si
/si-linux-amd64
# Stray committed test binary (11MB ELF, `go test -c`-style dropping from March,
# unstripped with debug_info). The live service runs ~/bin/si.
/si-test
si-chat/node_modules
si-chat/dist

# inber agent-session runtime state (session/memory DBs + materialized workspace);
# never source. Matches the canonical inber repo, which gitignores .inber/.
.inber/
